**Elevator pitch (30 words):**
> Dual-Lobe splits one AI task across two model processes with different powers: an Executor that acts and a Strategist that senses, critiques, authorizes, and verifies evidence — so success claims must be backed by proof.

**Long pitch (90 words):**
> Dual-Lobe is an open-source, drop-in OpenAI-compatible reverse proxy that enforces a dual-process cognitive architecture around any supported foundation model. An Executor Lobe streams responses and runs tools with zero critical-path wait. A Strategist Lobe reviews in the background, classifies material claims against supplied evidence, maintains versioned memory, and can take the conversation over in Director Mode. Four hard invariants — planning, action, verification, and escalation locks — make cooperation structural rather than polite. The core rule is simple: narrow evidence may support only a narrow claim.

**Positioning statement (formal):**
> Dual-Lobe is not a prompt hack and not a single model talking to itself. It is an engineering architecture with asymmetric tool authority, typed inter-lobe communication, append-only auditability, and an explicit anti-deception rule. It is designed to reduce false-success declarations, unauthorized side effects, correlated errors, and unrecoverable stalls in long-running AI agents. It is an advisory architecture, not a truth guarantee.

